SECTION F — OMS (ORDER MANAGEMENT SYSTEM)
OMS v3 State Machine (engine/internal/omsv3/aggregate.go)

StateNew → StateValidated → StateRiskApproved → StateSubmitted
                                                      ↓
StateRejected ← StateRiskBlocked      StateAcknowledged
     ↑                                      ↓
StateCancelled ←──────────────── StatePartiallyFilled
                                      ↓
                                  StateFilled (terminal)
State transition enforcement: ValidateTransition() returns ErrInvalidTransition — states cannot be skipped.

Idempotency: All events carry idempotency_key; ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING on insert.

Bypass Risk: EventRiskBlocked → StateRejected is terminal, meaning a blocked order cannot be resubmitted. However, a new order can be created immediately after — no cooldown on retry.

OMS Score: 78/100 — State machine solid, idempotency correct, but no broker reconciliation loop verified in source.

