4.2 Kelly Sizing Algorithm (Verified from riskv2/kelly.go)

Full Kelly = (b×p - q) / b
  where:
    b = avgWin / avgLoss  (reward/risk ratio)
    p = WinRate
    q = 1 - p

Stability = clamp((TotalTrades/100) × (ProfitFactor/1.5), 0, 1)

Mode selection:
  IF stability < 0.45 OR DDRisk > 0.6:
    Use QuarterKelly (25% of Full Kelly)
  ELSE:
    Use HalfKelly (50% of Full Kelly)

Output: RecommendedSizeBTC = selectedFraction × (equityUSD / price)
