16. AI HANDOVER BLUEPRINT
What This System Does
RAIG (Raig Algorithmic Intelligence Gateway) is an autonomous BTC/USDT scalping engine and Indian equity options trader. It runs 261+ registered strategies (plus expansion pack) simultaneously against live market data. All trading is currently paper-only on a $1,000,000 simulated account. The system is designed for eventual live capital deployment on Binance (BTC perpetuals), Delta Exchange (BTC options), and AngelOne (NSE/NIFTY).

Architecture in 5 Sentences
Go engine (engine/cmd/antigravity/main.go) is the single runtime: it ingests live BTC tick data via Coinbase WebSocket, evaluates 261+ strategies every candle close, enforces 4 institutional risk gates, and executes paper trades with full event sourcing to PostgreSQL.

Next.js BFF (client/, deployed to Vercel) provides 118 API routes proxying the Go engine, a dashboard UI, auth (JWT session cookie), and 2 daily cron jobs (strategy ranking, policy snapshot).

AI multi-agent system runs 4 LLM agents (Bull, Bear, Macro, Risk) in parallel every 5-minute candle, with 7-provider fallback chain (Groq→Gemini→Mistral→HuggingFace→Cloudflare→OpenRouter→OpenAI), producing advisory signals that are parked for human/bridge approval before execution.

Data layer uses 4 databases: PostgreSQL (Neon) for the event-sourced ledger, MongoDB (Atlas) for paper trading state, SQLite (embedded) for engine snapshots, and Redis (Upstash) for indicator cache.

Risk stack enforces 4 sequential gates (PMS portfolio budget → Pre-trade Risk V2 with Kelly sizing → Elite drawdown gate → Execution floor of 0.01 BTC) on every signal before any order is placed.

